@model string
@*
    Round 7B: the reCAPTCHA of an anonymous learner-portal form that creates or e-mails something, following the Account/Register standard:
    the same Google widget with the configured public site key (WebConfig.RecaptchaPublicKey, the model's SiteKey), the hidden
    GoogleReCaptchaResponse field the GoogleReCaptchaValidation attribute checks on the server, and the same behaviour when the keys are blank
    (the check is refused, as on Register). The page adds the api.js include and resgrid.recaptcha-field.js in its Scripts section.
*@
<div class="form-group">
    <div class="g-recaptcha" data-sitekey="@Model"></div>
    <input name="GoogleReCaptchaResponse" id="GoogleReCaptchaResponse" type="hidden" value="" />
</div>
